        "text": "This is definitive. The incoming relations confirm:\n- `HTAN_BIOSPECIMEN_ID` (`a2dd51c38aeb49e5ab37a3fd11371870`) \u2192 only belongs to **`biospecimen`** (`49d0227211654561b8738e61658ca4c1`)\n- `HTAN_PARENT_ID` (`08794222f9de4ea9baddc079c82ad51d`) \u2192 only belongs to **`biospecimen`** (`49d0227211654561b8738e61658ca4c1`)\n- `individualID` (`5d528d98d5b5417c8f53f2f263f82439`) \u2192 belongs to **`org.synapse.nf-biospecimentemplate`** (`7b8745f7b42c463c82aa8e85efdd70bb`) and several other NF types, but **NOT** to `biospecimen`\n- `tumorType` (`1bcf20e6579041039e9a773543756b99`) \u2192 belongs to **`org.synapse.nf-biospecimentemplate`** (`7b8745f7b42c463c82aa8e85efdd70bb`) and several other NF types, but **NOT** to `biospecimen`\n\n---\n\n## \u26a0\ufe0f Schema Mismatch \u2014 Mixed Fields from Two Distinct Schemas\n\nThe sample **cannot be matched to a single schema** in this project. Its four fields are drawn from **two separate, non-overlapping schemas**:\n\n---\n\n### Candidate A \u2014 `org.synapse.nf-biospecimentemplate`\n- **Node ID:** `7b8745f7b42c463c82aa8e85efdd70bb`\n- **Space:** `bcf12238fad04e229f21d8524219b72d` (NF/Synapse space)\n- **Matching fields from sample:**\n  - `individualID` \u2192 Element ID `5d528d98d5b5417c8f53f2f263f82439`\n  - `tumorType` \u2192 Element ID `1bcf20e6579041039e9a773543756b99`\n- **Missing from this schema:** `HTAN_BIOSPECIMEN_ID`, `HTAN_PARENT_ID`\n\n---\n\n### Candidate B \u2014 `biospecimen`\n- **Node ID:** `49d0227211654561b8738e61658ca4c1`\n- **Space:** `ff2a2c2588a04783a63b8e2983f4d407` (HTAN space)\n- **Matching fields from sample:**\n  - `HTAN_BIOSPECIMEN_ID` \u2192 Element ID `a2dd51c38aeb49e5ab37a3fd11371870`\n  - `HTAN_PARENT_ID` \u2192 Element ID `08794222f9de4ea9baddc079c82ad51d`\n- **Missing from this schema:** `individualID`, `tumorType`\n\n---\n\n### Conclusion\n\nThe sample **mixes fields from two distinct schemas** that live in different spaces:\n- `individualID` + `tumorType` belong exclusively to the **NF Synapse** biospecimen template (`org.synapse.nf-biospecimentemplate`, ID: `7b8745f7b42c463c82aa8e85efdd70bb`)\n- `HTAN_BIOSPECIMEN_ID` + `HTAN_PARENT_ID` belong exclusively to the **HTAN** biospecimen schema (`biospecimen`, ID: `49d0227211654561b8738e61658ca4c1`)\n\nNo single schema in the project contains all four fields. The data sample appears to be a **hybrid/merged record** combining NF-style individual/tumor metadata with HTAN biospecimen identifiers. You should verify whether this blending is intentional or represents a data quality issue.",
